# Re-include the curated README examples. The directory has to be un-excluded
# before the file pattern below can fire: git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, so a negation for a file inside one never matches. These are
# flux-schnell output, Apache-2.0 and publishable -- see docs/images/*.license.
!docs/images/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.png
!docs/images/*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.nsys-rep
*.sqlite
*.log
*.out
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.docx

# Comparison figures. This repository is public and FLUX.1-dev output is under a
# non-commercial licence, so dev-arm images must not be pushed. Rebuild with
# `make figures`; use the Apache-2.0 flux-schnell arm for anything public.
docs/figures/

# Site-specific operator runbook. Names an internal cluster, a storage volume,
# and a capacity reservation, so it stays local. Every finding in it that is
# transferable to anyone else lives in README.md or INSTALL.md instead.
RUNBOOK.md
RUNBOOK.docx
